version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-15"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22761195
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22761195
    description: "Concept DOI (resolves to the newest archived version; the 0.2.0 version DOI is minted by Zenodo when the GitHub Release is published)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22761196
    description: "Version DOI for 0.1.11 (the previous release)"
abstract: >-
  Fullseye is a numpy-native library of typed classical image-processing and
  geometric-vision operators (2-D and 3-D; 1,942 operators in the machine-readable index:
  918 2-D operators and 1,024 in the typed ledgers), with an evolutionary pipeline-design mode
  evaluated under honest held-out gates, a Physical-AI perception stack
  (stereo -> depth -> point cloud -> 6-DoF pose), and an HDevelop-style IDE
  (Fullseye Studio). Every operator carries a machine-readable Markdown note
  (contract, references, license, version fingerprint) designed to double as a
  retrieval corpus for AI assistants and as a reproducible, citable methods reference.
keywords:
  - image processing
  - machine vision
  - explainable algorithms
  - robotics perception
  - evolutionary computation
